WEBVTT

00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:17.198
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:19.443
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:20.758
The family business.

00:00:25.582 --> 00:00:27.043
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:00:27.044 --> 00:00:29.383
Having some stupid, macho showdown?!

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:30.713
I have a plan, Sam.

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:33.090
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:00:33.091 --> 00:00:34.386
I won't hunt this demon,

00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:36.541
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:00:36.735 --> 00:00:39.020
Did you really think you could trap me?

00:00:39.022 --> 00:00:41.345
Oh, I don't want to trap
you. I want to make a deal.

00:00:41.344 --> 00:00:43.276
I will give you the colt and the bullet,

00:00:43.278 --> 00:00:44.636
But you got to help Dean.

00:00:44.639 --> 00:00:45.991
You got to bring him back.

00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:48.521
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:51.153
Giving to Salomon, these protective
circles, they really work.

00:00:51.157 --> 00:00:54.201
You get a demon in one,
they're trapped, powerless.

00:03:35.188 --> 00:03:37.001
What's going on? Oh, my god.

00:03:39.348 --> 00:03:40.502
Get a doctor.

00:03:41.646 --> 00:03:42.923
Run!

00:03:44.668 --> 00:03:45.763
What happened?

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.312
Talk to me. Dogs.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:50.172
Stay with us, baby! Dogs... Black dogs.

00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:52.283
Robert?

00:03:52.726 --> 00:03:54.641
Robert, don't you die on me!

00:04:10.028 --> 00:04:11.692
So much for our low profile.

00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:15.030
You got a warrant in St. Louis, and now
you're officially in the feds' database.

00:04:15.045 --> 00:04:17.543
Dude, I'm like Dillinger or
something. Dean, it's not funny.

00:04:17.835 --> 00:04:19.901
It makes the job harder. We
got to be more careful now.

00:04:19.908 --> 00:04:21.023
What do they got on you?

00:04:23.658 --> 00:04:24.573
I'm sure they just

00:04:24.677 --> 00:04:27.120
Haven't posted it yet.
Well, you're no accessory,

00:04:27.177 --> 00:04:28.442
Nothing? Shut up.

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:31.122
You're jealous. No, I'm not!

00:04:31.127 --> 00:04:31.863
Uh-Huh.

00:04:33.777 --> 00:04:34.522
All right,

00:04:34.635 --> 00:04:37.551
What do you got on the case there,
you innocent, harmless young man, you?

00:04:40.955 --> 00:04:44.651
"Architect Sean Boyden plummeted to
his death from the roof of his home,

00:04:44.656 --> 00:04:46.373
A condominium he designed"

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:49.423
Build a high rise and
jump off. That's classy.

00:04:49.615 --> 00:04:51.013
When did he call animal control?

00:04:51.015 --> 00:04:52.093
Two days earlier.

00:04:52.096 --> 00:04:53.882
Did he actually say "black dog"? Yeah.

00:04:53.888 --> 00:04:56.233
"Vicious, wild, black dog"

00:04:56.397 --> 00:04:59.243
The authorities couldn't find
it, and no one else saw it.

00:04:59.488 --> 00:05:02.731
In fact, the authorities are a
little confused as to how a wild dog

00:05:02.737 --> 00:05:04.033
Could get past the doorman,

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.353
Take the elevator up, and start roaming
the halls of the cushiest joint in town.

00:05:07.488 --> 00:05:10.562
After that, no more calls.
He doesn't show up for work.

00:05:10.886 --> 00:05:12.571
Two days later, he takes a swan dive.

00:05:12.577 --> 00:05:14.472
You think we're dealing
with an actual black dog?

00:05:14.695 --> 00:05:16.781
Well, maybe. What's the lore on it?

00:05:16.785 --> 00:05:18.101
It's all pretty vague.

00:05:18.248 --> 00:05:20.752
There are spectral black
dogs all over the world, but

00:05:20.896 --> 00:05:23.520
Some say they're animal
spirits, others say death omens.

00:05:23.526 --> 00:05:25.023
But anyways, whatever they are, they're

00:05:25.385 --> 00:05:26.612
Big, nasty...

00:05:26.617 --> 00:05:28.931
Yeah, bet they could hump
the crap out of your leg.

00:05:28.937 --> 00:05:30.061
Look at that one. Huh?

00:05:32.026 --> 00:05:32.870
What? They could.

00:05:36.128 --> 00:05:36.941
So,

00:05:37.516 --> 00:05:39.952
You and Sean Boyden were
business partners for

00:05:40.446 --> 00:05:41.880
Almost 10 years, right?

00:05:42.198 --> 00:05:43.132
That's right.

00:05:43.135 --> 00:05:45.741
Now, one more time, this is
for... A tribute for Mr. Boyden,

00:05:45.747 --> 00:05:47.022
"Architectural Digest".

00:05:50.208 --> 00:05:51.820
Funny to you? No,

00:05:52.836 --> 00:05:53.693
It's just uh

00:05:53.857 --> 00:05:55.022
"Tribute".

00:05:55.856 --> 00:05:56.911
Yeah.

00:05:56.935 --> 00:05:59.003
See, Sean always got the tributes.

00:06:00.448 --> 00:06:01.713
He kills himself,

00:06:02.385 --> 00:06:04.052
Leaves me and his family behind,

00:06:04.526 --> 00:06:06.052
But he gets another tribute.

00:06:06.178 --> 00:06:07.023
Right.

00:06:08.196 --> 00:06:10.081
Any idea why he'd do such a thing?

00:06:10.676 --> 00:06:12.963
I have no clue. I mean,
he lived a charmed life.

00:06:13.376 --> 00:06:14.283
How so?

00:06:14.738 --> 00:06:16.303
He was a flat-Out genius.

00:06:16.585 --> 00:06:18.872
I mean, I'm capable,
but, next to him, uh...

00:06:20.238 --> 00:06:21.950
It wasn't always that way either.

00:06:22.117 --> 00:06:22.961
No?

00:06:24.468 --> 00:06:25.853
You  want to know the truth?

00:06:26.105 --> 00:06:28.553
There was a time where he
couldn't even design a pup tent.

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:31.740
Hell, 10 years ago, he was working
as a bartender at this place called

00:06:31.938 --> 00:06:32.830
Lloyd's,

00:06:32.977 --> 00:06:34.220
A complete dive.

00:06:34.448 --> 00:06:36.231
So, what changed? You got me.

00:06:36.458 --> 00:06:37.432
But overnight

00:06:37.788 --> 00:06:39.342
He gets this huge commission,

00:06:39.466 --> 00:06:40.893
And he starts designing...

00:06:42.277 --> 00:06:43.763
He starts designing the most

00:06:43.937 --> 00:06:45.370
Ingenious buildings

00:06:45.388 --> 00:06:47.480
Anyone has ever seen. It was like

00:06:47.635 --> 00:06:50.323
The level of Van Gogh and Mozart.

00:06:51.288 --> 00:06:52.023
What?

00:06:52.027 --> 00:06:53.243
It's funny.

00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:54.653
True geniuses, they...

00:06:55.115 --> 00:06:56.751
Seem to die young, don't they?

00:06:59.015 --> 00:06:59.971
To have

00:06:59.976 --> 00:07:02.141
That kind of talent...

00:07:02.486 --> 00:07:03.341
Why...

00:07:04.958 --> 00:07:06.262
Why just throw it away?

00:07:17.578 --> 00:07:18.412
So?

00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:20.480
The secretary's name is Carly.

00:07:20.918 --> 00:07:22.842
She's 23. She kayaks...

00:07:23.178 --> 00:07:23.991
And they're real.

00:07:23.997 --> 00:07:27.182
You didn't happen to ask her if she's
seen any black dogs lately, did you?

00:07:27.185 --> 00:07:28.683
Every complain called in this week

00:07:28.686 --> 00:07:31.902
About anything big, black, or
dog like. There's 19 calls in all,

00:07:31.907 --> 00:07:33.061
And, uh,

00:07:34.406 --> 00:07:35.482
I don't know what this is.

00:07:38.108 --> 00:07:39.621
You mean, Carly's my space address?

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:40.943
Yeah, my space. What the hell is that?

00:07:42.877 --> 00:07:44.641
Seriously, is that like
some sort of porn site?

00:07:49.366 --> 00:07:51.593
I swear, if this is
another freakin' pomeranian

00:07:51.598 --> 00:07:53.330
Barking in the neighbor's yard...

00:07:54.056 --> 00:07:55.280
Afternoon, ma'am.

00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:56.961
Animal control.

00:07:57.576 --> 00:07:59.420
Oh, someone already came yesterday.

00:07:59.425 --> 00:08:00.680
Oh, we're just following up.

00:08:01.117 --> 00:08:02.982
We're looking for Dr. Sylvia Perlman.

00:08:04.526 --> 00:08:05.442
The  doctor,

00:08:05.456 --> 00:08:06.581
Well, she...

00:08:07.098 --> 00:08:09.760
I don't know exactly when she'll
be back. She left two days ago.

00:08:09.807 --> 00:08:10.640
Okay.

00:08:10.677 --> 00:08:11.601
And you are?

00:08:11.646 --> 00:08:12.730
I'm Miss Perlman's maid.

00:08:12.735 --> 00:08:14.000
So, where did the doctor go?

00:08:14.005 --> 00:08:14.871
I'm not sure.

00:08:15.187 --> 00:08:17.373
She just packed and went.
She didn't say where.

00:08:17.715 --> 00:08:19.493
That stray dog, did you find it finally?

00:08:19.695 --> 00:08:20.951
Uh, not yet.

00:08:21.135 --> 00:08:21.980
You know,

00:08:21.986 --> 00:08:24.562
You didn't ever happen to
see the dog yourself, did you?

00:08:24.855 --> 00:08:27.583
Well, no. I never even heard it.

00:08:27.855 --> 00:08:30.611
I was almost starting to think the
doctor was imagining things, but

00:08:30.618 --> 00:08:33.432
She's not like that, so...
You know, I read she was

00:08:33.436 --> 00:08:35.103
The chief surgeon at the hospital.

00:08:35.526 --> 00:08:38.510
So she's got to be, what, 42, 43?
That's pretty young for that job.

00:08:38.515 --> 00:08:39.990
Youngest in the history of the place.

00:08:40.172 --> 00:08:42.245
She got the position 10 years ago.

00:08:44.584 --> 00:08:46.896
An overnight success, 10 years ago.

00:08:47.088 --> 00:08:48.496
Yeah, we know a guy like that.

00:08:49.709 --> 00:08:50.882
Oh, look at this.

00:08:54.556 --> 00:08:55.540
Lloyd's bar.

00:09:23.476 --> 00:09:24.553
Miss Perlman?

00:09:25.305 --> 00:09:26.840
I've been calling for hours!

00:09:27.107 --> 00:09:30.203
You need to vacate the room,
or you got to pay for the night!

00:09:34.165 --> 00:09:35.091
Okay,

00:09:35.215 --> 00:09:36.213
No problem.

00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:19.121
H ey.

00:10:19.915 --> 00:10:20.701
Yeah?

00:10:21.585 --> 00:10:22.601
That's weird.

00:10:23.338 --> 00:10:25.283
What? Think someone planted these?

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:30.441
In the middle of all these weeds?

00:10:30.807 --> 00:10:32.270
These are, uh, what do you call them?

00:10:32.278 --> 00:10:33.652
Yarrow flowers? Yeah.

00:10:33.655 --> 00:10:35.421
Used for certain rituals, aren't they?

00:10:35.786 --> 00:10:38.072
Yeah, actually, summoning rituals.

00:10:40.998 --> 00:10:41.770
So,

00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:45.402
Two people become sudden
successes about 10 years ago,

00:10:45.407 --> 00:10:47.540
Right around the time they were
hanging out here at Lloyd's.

00:10:47.556 --> 00:10:49.433
Where there just happens
to be a crossroads.

00:10:49.508 --> 00:10:51.002
You think? Let's find out.

00:10:57.915 --> 00:10:59.413
Seem about the dead center to you?

00:11:06.836 --> 00:11:07.690
Yahtzee.

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:24.901
I'd be willing to bet
that's graveyard dirt.

00:11:26.407 --> 00:11:30.220
And a black cat bone.
That's serious spellwork.

00:11:30.576 --> 00:11:32.320
I mean, that's deep south hoodoo stuff.

00:11:32.335 --> 00:11:34.153
Used to summon a demon.

00:11:35.285 --> 00:11:36.670
Not just summon one.

00:11:37.566 --> 00:11:39.333
Crossroad's where pacts are made.

00:11:40.186 --> 00:11:43.062
These people are actually making
deals with the damned thing.

00:11:43.566 --> 00:11:45.082
You know, 'cause that always ends good.

00:11:46.667 --> 00:11:48.203
They're seeing dogs, all right...

00:11:49.195 --> 00:11:51.623
But not black dogs.
They're seeing hellhounds,

00:11:52.056 --> 00:11:53.761
Demonic pit bulls.

00:11:53.766 --> 00:11:56.832
Whoever this demon is, it's
back and it's collecting.

00:11:57.005 --> 00:11:59.451
And that doctor lady,
wherever she's running,

00:12:00.095 --> 00:12:01.771
She ain't running fast enough.

00:13:24.147 --> 00:13:25.300
Holy...

00:13:25.615 --> 00:13:26.760
Holy?

00:13:30.236 --> 00:13:31.363
Guess again.

00:13:31.938 --> 00:13:34.790
<i>Now save poor bob, if you please</i>

00:13:38.346 --> 00:13:40.052
I want to play guitar.

00:13:41.187 --> 00:13:44.072
I want you to make me the
best blues man ever lived.

00:13:45.427 --> 00:13:47.051
If that's what you want...

00:13:50.998 --> 00:13:51.802
So...

00:13:52.287 --> 00:13:53.260
How...

00:13:53.655 --> 00:13:54.920
Do we shake on it?

00:14:24.987 --> 00:14:27.380
So, it's just like the
Robert Johnson legend, right?

00:14:27.797 --> 00:14:30.083
I mean, "selling your soul at the
crossroads", that kind of deal?

00:14:30.086 --> 00:14:31.571
Except that wasn't a legend.

00:14:31.647 --> 00:14:33.011
You know his music.

00:14:34.777 --> 00:14:36.321
You don't know Robert Johnson songs?

00:14:36.596 --> 00:14:39.241
Sam, there's occult
references all over his lyrics.

00:14:39.255 --> 00:14:40.881
I mean, "Crossroad blues,"

00:14:41.118 --> 00:14:42.470
"Me and the Devil blues,"

00:14:42.478 --> 00:14:43.902
"Hellhound on my Trail"?

00:14:45.996 --> 00:14:48.250
Story  goes that he died
choking on his own blood.

00:14:48.255 --> 00:14:51.993
He was hallucinating and
muttering about big, evil dogs.

00:14:52.838 --> 00:14:54.330
And now it's happening all over again.

00:14:54.338 --> 00:14:55.182
Yeah.

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:58.093
We got to find out if anyone else
struck any bargains around here.

00:14:58.197 --> 00:14:59.040
Right,

00:14:59.046 --> 00:15:00.852
So, we got to clean up
these people's mess for them?

00:15:00.856 --> 00:15:02.812
They're not exactly squeaky-Clean.

00:15:03.017 --> 00:15:05.691
Nobody put a gun to their head and
forced them to play "let's make a deal".

00:15:05.697 --> 00:15:07.491
So, what, we should
just leave them to die?

00:15:07.497 --> 00:15:10.210
Somebody goes over Niagara in a barrel,
you gonna jump in to try to save them?

00:15:10.215 --> 00:15:10.983
Dean...

00:15:12.967 --> 00:15:13.761
All right...

00:15:14.547 --> 00:15:15.573
Fine.

00:15:17.205 --> 00:15:19.700
Rituals like this, you got to put
your own photo into the mix, right?

00:15:19.705 --> 00:15:21.871
So this guy probably summoned the thing.

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:23.812
Let's see if anyone inside knows him...

00:15:24.716 --> 00:15:25.750
If he's still alive.

00:15:33.868 --> 00:15:36.052
What's this guy's name,
again? George Darrow.

00:15:36.056 --> 00:15:38.230
Apparent quite the regular at Lloyd's.

00:15:39.188 --> 00:15:42.770
This house probably ain't up
next on "mtv cribs", is it?

00:15:42.777 --> 00:15:43.733
Yeah.

00:15:43.735 --> 00:15:45.341
So, whatever kind of deal he made...

00:15:45.356 --> 00:15:46.682
Wasn't for cash.

00:15:46.917 --> 00:15:50.093
Ah, who knows? Maybe his place is
full of babes in princess Leia bikinis.

00:15:51.518 --> 00:15:52.892
I'm just saying,

00:15:52.908 --> 00:15:55.383
This guy's got one epic bill come due.

00:15:55.675 --> 00:15:57.501
Hope at least he asked
for something fun.

00:16:04.348 --> 00:16:05.281
Look at that.

00:16:11.846 --> 00:16:12.902
What is that, pepper?

00:16:16.788 --> 00:16:18.740
Who the hell are you? George Darrow?

00:16:19.358 --> 00:16:21.012
I'm not buying anything.
Whoa, looks like

00:16:21.106 --> 00:16:22.581
You  went for the wrong shaker, there.

00:16:23.456 --> 00:16:26.090
Usually, when you want to keep
something evil out, you go for the salt.

00:16:28.675 --> 00:16:30.240
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:16:30.466 --> 00:16:31.610
Talking about this.

00:16:35.507 --> 00:16:36.603
Tell me...

00:16:36.808 --> 00:16:38.190
You seen that hellhound yet?

00:16:38.846 --> 00:16:39.651
Look,

00:16:40.258 --> 00:16:41.110
We want to help.

00:16:41.117 --> 00:16:42.263
Please,

00:16:42.818 --> 00:16:43.991
Just 5 minutes.

00:16:57.338 --> 00:16:58.991
So, what is that stuff out front?

00:16:59.385 --> 00:17:00.670
Goofer dust.

00:17:03.458 --> 00:17:07.113
What, you boys think you know something
about something, but not goofer dust?

00:17:12.405 --> 00:17:14.640
Well, we know a little
about a lot of things,

00:17:14.645 --> 00:17:16.541
Just enough to make us dangerous.

00:17:17.497 --> 00:17:18.430
What is it?

00:17:18.927 --> 00:17:19.821
Hoodoo.

00:17:20.905 --> 00:17:22.322
My grandma taught me.

00:17:22.817 --> 00:17:24.292
Keeps out demons.

00:17:24.606 --> 00:17:25.731
Demons, we know.

00:17:25.877 --> 00:17:26.971
Well, then,

00:17:27.256 --> 00:17:28.191
Keep it.

00:17:28.736 --> 00:17:30.772
Maybe it'll do you some good.

00:17:34.067 --> 00:17:35.963
4 minutes left.

00:17:39.035 --> 00:17:40.483
Mr. Darrow...

00:17:41.208 --> 00:17:44.221
We know you're in trouble.
Yeah, that you got yourself into.

00:17:45.466 --> 00:17:47.863
But it's not hopeless, all right?

00:17:48.345 --> 00:17:49.731
There's got to be something we can do.

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:50.592
Listen,

00:17:51.007 --> 00:17:52.961
I get that you boys want to help,

00:17:54.055 --> 00:17:58.711
But sometimes a person makes their bed
and they just got to lie down in it.

00:18:01.797 --> 00:18:04.571
I'm the one called that
demon in the first place.

00:18:05.227 --> 00:18:07.041
What'd you do it for? I was weak.

00:18:08.215 --> 00:18:09.991
I mean, who don't want to be great?

00:18:10.727 --> 00:18:13.071
Who don't want their
life to mean something?

00:18:15.066 --> 00:18:15.940
I just...

00:18:17.438 --> 00:18:19.601
I just never thought about the price.

00:18:19.925 --> 00:18:20.853
Was it worth it?

00:18:20.857 --> 00:18:22.100
Hell, no

00:18:23.076 --> 00:18:24.793
Course, I asked for talent.

00:18:25.265 --> 00:18:27.033
Should have gone for fame.

00:18:28.407 --> 00:18:30.240
I'm still broke...

00:18:30.775 --> 00:18:32.001
And lonely.

00:18:32.195 --> 00:18:35.093
Just now I got this pile of
paintings don't nobody want.

00:18:37.536 --> 00:18:39.352
That wasn't the worst.

00:18:43.097 --> 00:18:44.051
Go on.

00:18:45.436 --> 00:18:47.000
Demon didn't leave.

00:18:47.398 --> 00:18:48.912
I never counted on that.

00:18:48.995 --> 00:18:52.462
After our deal was done, the damn
thing stayed at Lloyd's for a week,

00:18:52.755 --> 00:18:53.993
Just chatting,

00:18:54.567 --> 00:18:56.221
Making more deals.

00:18:57.628 --> 00:18:59.373
I tried to warn folks, but

00:18:59.968 --> 00:19:01.823
Who gonna listen to an old drunk?

00:19:01.827 --> 00:19:03.171
How many others are there?

00:19:03.595 --> 00:19:05.021
This architect,

00:19:05.498 --> 00:19:08.670
A doctor lady. I kept up with
them. They've been in the papers.

00:19:10.426 --> 00:19:12.111
At least they got famous.

00:19:13.276 --> 00:19:14.960
Who else, George? Come on, think.

00:19:15.445 --> 00:19:16.741
Oh, one more.

00:19:18.487 --> 00:19:19.883
Uh, nice guy, too.

00:19:21.506 --> 00:19:22.430
Hudson,

00:19:23.147 --> 00:19:24.381
Evan I think.

00:19:25.258 --> 00:19:27.071
I don't know what he asked for.

00:19:28.406 --> 00:19:29.852
Don't matter now.

00:19:29.865 --> 00:19:31.240
We're done for.

00:19:32.276 --> 00:19:33.280
No.

00:19:33.787 --> 00:19:35.751
No, there's got to be
a way. You don't get it.

00:19:36.205 --> 00:19:37.651
I don't want a way.

00:19:38.278 --> 00:19:41.050
Look, you don't... I called that thing!

00:19:41.348 --> 00:19:43.091
I brought it on myself!

00:19:44.726 --> 00:19:46.131
I brought it on them.

00:19:47.657 --> 00:19:49.571
I'm going to hell,

00:19:49.576 --> 00:19:50.902
One way or another.

00:19:52.798 --> 00:19:54.952
All I want is to
finish my last painting.

00:19:55.708 --> 00:19:57.631
Day or two, I'm done.

00:19:58.138 --> 00:20:00.602
I'm just trying to
hold him off till then,

00:20:01.736 --> 00:20:03.273
Buy a little time.

00:20:04.426 --> 00:20:07.852
Okay, boys, time you went. Go
help somebody that wants help.

00:20:07.855 --> 00:20:09.861
We can't just... Get out!

00:20:10.608 --> 00:20:11.932
I got work to do.

00:20:12.725 --> 00:20:14.571
You don't really want to die.

00:20:15.827 --> 00:20:16.883
I don't?

00:20:24.017 --> 00:20:25.273
I'm tired.

00:21:01.486 --> 00:21:02.521
Evan?

00:21:02.758 --> 00:21:04.782
Are you spying on the neighbors?

00:21:05.648 --> 00:21:07.172
No, I, uh,

00:21:07.177 --> 00:21:09.562
I thought I heard something
in the yard, but it's nothing.

00:21:11.045 --> 00:21:12.283
You all ready to go?

00:21:12.297 --> 00:21:16.112
You know, if I didn't know better, I'd
say that you want me out of the house.

00:21:16.745 --> 00:21:19.121
Of course not. It's just, you've...

00:21:19.326 --> 00:21:21.823
You've barely seen your
sister since she had the baby.

00:21:21.828 --> 00:21:23.432
Well, what are you
going to do all weekend?

00:21:24.857 --> 00:21:28.363
Um, not much. I got some bills to pay.

00:21:33.327 --> 00:21:34.823
Come here.

00:21:39.048 --> 00:21:40.103
I'll miss you.

00:21:40.106 --> 00:21:41.192
You better.

00:21:44.955 --> 00:21:46.262
You know I love you, right?

00:21:46.725 --> 00:21:47.700
Forever.

00:21:48.647 --> 00:21:50.643
Of course. Evan, are you okay?

00:21:51.566 --> 00:21:52.671
Yeah.

00:21:54.217 --> 00:21:55.701
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:21:56.887 --> 00:21:58.023
Now, get going.

00:22:00.297 --> 00:22:01.933
Okay, I'll call you when I get there.

00:22:04.258 --> 00:22:05.432
Hey, sweetie?

00:22:13.135 --> 00:22:14.371
I love you, too.

00:22:26.317 --> 00:22:27.882
Yes? Evan Hudson?

00:22:27.886 --> 00:22:28.630
Yeah.

00:22:28.635 --> 00:22:30.463
You ever been to a bar called Lloyd's?

00:22:30.557 --> 00:22:32.253
Would have been about 10 years ago.

00:22:33.987 --> 00:22:36.342
Come on, we're not demons.

00:22:38.146 --> 00:22:39.543
Any other bright ideas?

00:23:05.988 --> 00:23:06.722
Evan?

00:23:06.726 --> 00:23:07.701
Please!

00:23:08.306 --> 00:23:09.290
Don't hurt me.

00:23:09.298 --> 00:23:11.602
We're not gonna hurt you, all
right? We're here to help you.

00:23:11.808 --> 00:23:13.652
We know all about the
genius deal you made.

00:23:14.107 --> 00:23:14.973
What?

00:23:15.575 --> 00:23:17.023
How? Doesn't matter.

00:23:17.575 --> 00:23:19.043
All that matters is
we're trying to stop it.

00:23:19.046 --> 00:23:20.882
How do I know you're not
lying? Well, you don't.

00:23:20.885 --> 00:23:22.822
But you're kind of running low
on options, there, buddy boy.

00:23:28.875 --> 00:23:29.881
Can you stop it?

00:23:29.885 --> 00:23:30.751
Don't know.

00:23:30.906 --> 00:23:32.050
We'll try.

00:23:33.956 --> 00:23:35.153
I don't wanna die.

00:23:35.348 --> 00:23:37.033
Of course you don't. Not now. Dean...

00:23:37.278 --> 00:23:39.042
Stop. What'd you ask for, anyway, Ev?

00:23:39.048 --> 00:23:39.772
Huh?

00:23:40.417 --> 00:23:42.791
Never need viagra, bowl
a perfect game, what?

00:23:45.917 --> 00:23:46.942
My wife.

00:23:48.767 --> 00:23:51.170
Right, getting the girl.
That's worth a trip to hell for.

00:23:51.177 --> 00:23:52.751
Dean, stop. No.

00:23:54.085 --> 00:23:55.293
He's right. I made the deal.

00:23:57.615 --> 00:23:59.453
Nobody twisted my arm. That, uh,

00:23:59.966 --> 00:24:00.900
Woman,

00:24:02.056 --> 00:24:05.040
Or whatever she was, at the bar, she
said I could have anything I wanted.

00:24:05.047 --> 00:24:07.081
I thought she was nuts, at first, but...

00:24:12.708 --> 00:24:13.831
I don't know. I was...

00:24:15.007 --> 00:24:16.151
I was desperate.

00:24:16.878 --> 00:24:17.792
Desperate?

00:24:24.296 --> 00:24:25.792
Julie  was dying.

00:24:31.386 --> 00:24:32.600
You did it to save her?

00:24:35.296 --> 00:24:37.083
She had cancer. They
had stopped treatment.

00:24:37.096 --> 00:24:39.551
They were moving her into
hospice. They kept saying,

00:24:40.276 --> 00:24:41.652
"Matter of days".

00:24:44.306 --> 00:24:45.543
So, yeah, I made the deal...

00:24:46.077 --> 00:24:47.333
And I'd do it again.

00:24:47.698 --> 00:24:49.342
I'd have died for her on the spot.

00:24:54.035 --> 00:24:55.511
Did you ever think
about her in all this?

00:24:55.516 --> 00:24:57.010
I did this for her.

00:24:57.018 --> 00:24:58.252
You sure about that?

00:25:00.067 --> 00:25:01.552
I think you did it for yourself...

00:25:02.946 --> 00:25:04.472
So you wouldn't have
to live without her.

00:25:05.977 --> 00:25:08.061
But, guess what, she's gonna
have to live without you now.

00:25:11.487 --> 00:25:13.503
What if she knew how much it cost?

00:25:14.907 --> 00:25:16.633
What if she knew it cost your soul?

00:25:17.078 --> 00:25:18.341
How do you think she'd feel?

00:25:19.418 --> 00:25:21.361
Okay, that's enough. Evan,

00:25:21.527 --> 00:25:22.720
Sit tight, all right?

00:25:22.888 --> 00:25:24.100
We're gonna figure this out.

00:25:32.927 --> 00:25:34.803
You all right? Why wouldn't I be?

00:25:36.325 --> 00:25:37.502
Hey, I got an idea.

00:25:38.617 --> 00:25:40.330
You throw George's
hoodoo at that hellhound,

00:25:40.338 --> 00:25:42.161
Keep it away from Evan
as long as you can.

00:25:42.828 --> 00:25:44.750
I'm gonna go to the crossroads
and summon the demon.

00:25:44.757 --> 00:25:45.630
Summon...

00:25:46.128 --> 00:25:47.100
Are you nuts?

00:25:47.556 --> 00:25:49.050
Maybe a little.

00:25:49.395 --> 00:25:50.723
But I can trap it.

00:25:50.885 --> 00:25:53.711
I can exorcise it and I can buy us time
to figure out something more permanent.

00:25:53.716 --> 00:25:56.092
Yeah, but how much time?
I don't know. A while.

00:25:56.315 --> 00:25:59.491
It's not easy for those suckers to claw their
way back from hell and into the sunshine.

00:25:59.495 --> 00:26:00.241
No.

00:26:00.245 --> 00:26:01.710
No way. Not allowed to say no, Sammy,

00:26:01.716 --> 00:26:03.970
Unless you got a better idea.
Dean, you can forget it, all right?

00:26:03.985 --> 00:26:05.653
I'm not letting you
summon that demon. Why not?

00:26:05.658 --> 00:26:07.692
Because I don't like where your
head is at right now. That's why not.

00:26:07.725 --> 00:26:09.473
What are you talking about?
You've been on edge ever since

00:26:09.477 --> 00:26:11.630
We found that crossroads,
Dean, and I think I know why.

00:26:11.646 --> 00:26:13.562
We don't have time for this. Dad.

00:26:15.575 --> 00:26:18.231
You think maybe dad made
one of these deals, huh?

00:26:20.716 --> 00:26:21.520
Hell,

00:26:21.568 --> 00:26:22.990
I've been thinking it.

00:26:23.597 --> 00:26:25.230
I'm sure you've been thinking it, too.

00:26:33.256 --> 00:26:34.521
It fits, doesn't it?

00:26:36.026 --> 00:26:37.830
I'm alive, dad's dead.

00:26:38.057 --> 00:26:39.663
Yellow-Eyed demon was involved.

00:26:41.805 --> 00:26:42.923
What if he did?

00:26:44.425 --> 00:26:45.712
What if he struck a deal?

00:26:47.216 --> 00:26:48.591
My life for his soul.

00:26:52.165 --> 00:26:54.202
<i>Hey, guys, I think I
hear it! It's outside!</i>

00:26:54.398 --> 00:26:56.013
Just keep him alive, okay?

00:26:57.348 --> 00:26:58.672
Dean? Go!

00:27:24.705 --> 00:27:25.653
So,

00:27:25.927 --> 00:27:28.781
What brings a guy like
you to a place like this?

00:27:31.486 --> 00:27:32.721
You called me?

00:27:32.965 --> 00:27:34.382
I'm just glad it worked.

00:27:36.206 --> 00:27:37.330
First time?

00:27:38.915 --> 00:27:40.051
You could say that.

00:27:40.457 --> 00:27:42.000
Oh, come on, now.

00:27:42.395 --> 00:27:44.242
Don't sell yourself short.

00:27:44.568 --> 00:27:46.962
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:27:49.725 --> 00:27:51.243
So you know who I am.

00:27:51.477 --> 00:27:52.862
I get the newsletter.

00:27:53.005 --> 00:27:54.841
Well, don't keep me in suspense.

00:27:55.355 --> 00:27:56.533
What have you heard?

00:27:57.067 --> 00:27:58.152
Well,

00:27:58.255 --> 00:28:00.371
I heard you were handsome.

00:28:01.206 --> 00:28:02.480
You're just edible.

00:28:03.627 --> 00:28:05.722
What can I do for you, Dean?

00:28:08.316 --> 00:28:10.301
Maybe we should do this in my car.

00:28:11.025 --> 00:28:12.171
Nice and private.

00:28:12.176 --> 00:28:13.940
Sounds good to me.

00:28:30.386 --> 00:28:32.980
What is that stuff? Goofer dust.

00:28:33.036 --> 00:28:34.381
Are you serious?

00:28:34.935 --> 00:28:36.713
Yeah. Afraid so.

00:28:37.545 --> 00:28:40.250
Look, believe me, don't
believe me... Whatever you want.

00:28:40.257 --> 00:28:41.771
Just whatever you do,

00:28:41.965 --> 00:28:44.102
Stay inside this circle, all right?

00:28:45.348 --> 00:28:47.622
So, I was hoping we could strike a deal.

00:28:47.628 --> 00:28:49.220
That's what I do.

00:28:49.486 --> 00:28:52.302
I want Evan Hudson
released from his contract.

00:28:53.196 --> 00:28:55.040
So sorry, darling.

00:28:55.348 --> 00:28:57.261
That's not negotiable.

00:28:57.527 --> 00:28:59.221
I'll make it worth your while.

00:28:59.558 --> 00:29:00.972
Oh, really?

00:29:01.255 --> 00:29:03.140
What are you offering? Me.

00:29:06.186 --> 00:29:08.282
Well, well, well.

00:29:09.136 --> 00:29:11.583
You'd sacrifice your
life for someone else's.

00:29:12.847 --> 00:29:14.681
Like father, like son.

00:29:21.756 --> 00:29:23.403
That's the last of it.

00:29:24.266 --> 00:29:27.180
You did know about
your dad's deal, right?

00:29:27.307 --> 00:29:29.020
His life for yours.

00:29:30.795 --> 00:29:33.333
Oh, I didn't make the deal myself, but,

00:29:33.488 --> 00:29:35.750
Boy, I wish I had.

00:29:41.517 --> 00:29:42.631
After you.

00:29:42.635 --> 00:29:44.282
Such a gentleman.

00:29:48.885 --> 00:29:50.163
A devil's trap?

00:29:50.427 --> 00:29:52.872
You've got to be kidding me.

00:29:53.586 --> 00:29:54.423
What?

00:29:54.427 --> 00:29:55.503
You hear that?

00:29:55.825 --> 00:29:57.071
No. Where?

00:29:59.366 --> 00:30:00.990
Right outside the door.

00:30:14.286 --> 00:30:15.652
Just don't move, all right?

00:30:15.656 --> 00:30:17.100
Stay where you are.

00:30:20.747 --> 00:30:23.103
You stupid, stupid...

00:30:23.648 --> 00:30:25.561
I should rip you limb from limb.

00:30:25.568 --> 00:30:26.762
Take your best shot.

00:30:29.388 --> 00:30:30.630
No,

00:30:31.216 --> 00:30:32.660
I don't think so.

00:30:33.255 --> 00:30:35.061
I'm not gonna put you
out of your misery.

00:30:35.067 --> 00:30:35.981
Yeah? Why not?

00:30:35.995 --> 00:30:37.941
'Cause your misery is the whole point.

00:30:38.047 --> 00:30:39.951
It's too much fun to watch.

00:30:40.937 --> 00:30:43.430
Knowing how your daddy died for you,

00:30:43.438 --> 00:30:45.232
How he sold his soul.

00:30:45.357 --> 00:30:46.472
I mean,

00:30:46.477 --> 00:30:47.983
That's got to hurt.

00:30:50.597 --> 00:30:52.521
He's all you ever think about.

00:30:52.525 --> 00:30:54.551
You wake up, and your first thought is

00:30:54.556 --> 00:30:56.603
"I can't do this anymore".

00:30:56.848 --> 00:30:58.810
You're all lit up with pain.

00:30:59.008 --> 00:31:03.110
I mean, you loved him so
much. And it's all your fault.

00:31:05.268 --> 00:31:06.900
You blew it, Dean.

00:31:07.238 --> 00:31:08.852
I could have given you what you need.

00:31:08.856 --> 00:31:10.260
What do I need?

00:31:11.727 --> 00:31:12.940
Your father.

00:31:14.597 --> 00:31:16.351
I could have brought him back.

00:31:17.715 --> 00:31:19.041
Your loss.

00:31:19.585 --> 00:31:20.831
See ya, Dean.

00:31:20.835 --> 00:31:23.192
I wish you a nice, long life.

00:31:32.918 --> 00:31:33.902
Hold on.

00:31:56.685 --> 00:31:57.842
Do you still hear it?

00:31:58.487 --> 00:31:59.383
No.

00:31:59.778 --> 00:32:00.820
Is it over?

00:32:07.436 --> 00:32:08.682
It's here!

00:32:15.366 --> 00:32:19.581
You're lucky I've got a soft spot
for lost puppies and long faces.

00:32:20.938 --> 00:32:23.341
I just can't leave you like this.

00:32:23.635 --> 00:32:24.952
Besides,

00:32:24.968 --> 00:32:27.283
You didn't call me here
to bargain for Evan.

00:32:27.445 --> 00:32:28.681
Not really.

00:32:28.696 --> 00:32:30.302
Can you bring him back?

00:32:31.046 --> 00:32:32.272
My dad?

00:32:33.127 --> 00:32:34.621
Of course I can,

00:32:34.636 --> 00:32:36.400
Just as he was.

00:32:37.267 --> 00:32:39.692
Your dad would live
a long, natural life,

00:32:39.838 --> 00:32:41.461
Like he was meant to.

00:32:42.026 --> 00:32:44.260
That's a promise. What about me?

00:32:44.266 --> 00:32:46.201
I could give you 10 years,

00:32:46.208 --> 00:32:49.072
10 long, good years with him.

00:32:49.277 --> 00:32:50.893
That's a lifetime.

00:32:51.118 --> 00:32:52.942
The family could be together again.

00:32:52.957 --> 00:32:55.271
John, Dean, Sammy...

00:32:55.665 --> 00:32:58.580
The Winchester boys all reunited.

00:33:03.148 --> 00:33:03.920
Look,

00:33:04.208 --> 00:33:06.250
Your dad is supposed to be alive.

00:33:07.215 --> 00:33:08.841
You're supposed to be dead.

00:33:09.648 --> 00:33:11.723
So, we'll just set things straight,

00:33:12.177 --> 00:33:14.511
Put things back in their natural order,

00:33:14.836 --> 00:33:17.323
And you get 10 extra years on top.

00:33:17.817 --> 00:33:19.553
That's a bonus.

00:33:28.415 --> 00:33:29.530
You think you could...

00:33:36.087 --> 00:33:37.681
Throw in a set of steak knives?

00:33:39.727 --> 00:33:42.991
You know, this smartass
self-Sefense mechanism of yours...

00:33:50.146 --> 00:33:51.500
Dean...

00:33:51.506 --> 00:33:53.011
Now you're really trapped.

00:33:54.026 --> 00:33:54.901
That's got to hurt.

00:33:54.908 --> 00:33:57.491
Let me out now.

00:33:57.495 --> 00:33:58.251
Sure.

00:33:58.256 --> 00:34:00.820
We just got to make a
little deal here first.

00:34:00.825 --> 00:34:02.603
You call off your hellhound

00:34:02.737 --> 00:34:04.041
And let Evan go.

00:34:04.868 --> 00:34:06.092
Then I'll let you go.

00:34:06.685 --> 00:34:09.253
I can't break a binding contract.

00:34:10.276 --> 00:34:12.180
And by "can't," you
mean "don't want to"?

00:34:13.395 --> 00:34:14.673
Last chance.

00:34:15.517 --> 00:34:18.120
Evan and his wife get to
live to a ripe old age.

00:34:18.695 --> 00:34:19.801
Going...

00:34:20.276 --> 00:34:22.011
Going... Let's talk about this.

00:34:22.016 --> 00:34:22.931
Okay, gone.

00:34:26.265 --> 00:34:27.451
Stay inside the circle!

00:34:37.316 --> 00:34:38.870
Come on, Dean...

00:34:40.777 --> 00:34:41.793
What are you doing?

00:34:41.878 --> 00:34:43.522
Oh, you're just gonna
go on a little trip.

00:34:45.818 --> 00:34:46.970
Way down south.

00:34:46.977 --> 00:34:48.941
Look, forget Evan. Think of your dad.

00:34:52.976 --> 00:34:54.231
Regna terrae,

00:34:54.475 --> 00:34:56.850
Cantate deo, psallite domino.

00:34:57.307 --> 00:34:59.603
Qui fertur super caelum caeli

00:34:59.617 --> 00:35:01.181
Ad orientem,

00:35:01.188 --> 00:35:04.620
Ecce dabit vocem suam, vocem virtutis.

00:35:04.628 --> 00:35:06.983
Tribuite virtutem deo.

00:35:06.987 --> 00:35:10.003
Qui fertur super caelum
caeli ad orientem,

00:35:15.048 --> 00:35:16.680
Circle's broken! Come on!

00:35:22.766 --> 00:35:24.010
Omnis fallaciae,

00:35:24.328 --> 00:35:26.231
Libera nos domine.

00:35:31.546 --> 00:35:33.723
Hostis humanae salutis.

00:35:36.626 --> 00:35:38.041
Wait!

00:36:02.618 --> 00:36:04.000
What the hell was that for?

00:36:04.127 --> 00:36:05.531
Sealing the deal.

00:36:05.536 --> 00:36:06.811
I usually like to be warned

00:36:06.817 --> 00:36:08.801
Before I'm violated with demon tongue.

00:36:08.877 --> 00:36:10.583
Evan Hudson is free.

00:36:10.856 --> 00:36:14.031
He and his wife will live long
lives. How do I know you're not lying?

00:36:14.036 --> 00:36:16.090
My word is my bond. Oh, really?

00:36:16.095 --> 00:36:17.861
It is when I make a deal.

00:36:18.145 --> 00:36:19.613
It's the rules.

00:36:20.546 --> 00:36:22.150
You got what you wanted.

00:36:22.555 --> 00:36:23.941
Now let me go.

00:36:34.917 --> 00:36:37.182
You're gonna double-Cross me?

00:36:37.258 --> 00:36:39.622
Funny how I'm the trustworthy one.

00:36:41.767 --> 00:36:43.351
You know,

00:36:43.575 --> 00:36:46.150
You renege, send me to hell,

00:36:46.168 --> 00:36:48.592
Sooner or later I'm gonna climb out, and

00:36:48.596 --> 00:36:51.431
Skinning Evan Hudson will
be the first thing that I do.

00:37:09.868 --> 00:37:11.040
I got to tell you,

00:37:11.465 --> 00:37:13.752
You would have never pulled
that stunt if you knew.

00:37:13.756 --> 00:37:14.551
Knew what?

00:37:14.898 --> 00:37:16.613
Where your dad is.

00:37:17.148 --> 00:37:18.732
You should have made that deal.

00:37:19.437 --> 00:37:21.332
See, people talk about hell,

00:37:21.577 --> 00:37:22.891
But it's just a word.

00:37:23.096 --> 00:37:25.740
Doesn't even come close
to describing the real...

00:37:25.746 --> 00:37:28.431
Shut your mouth, bitch! If
you could see your poor daddy,

00:37:28.438 --> 00:37:30.622
Hear the sounds he makes
'cause he can't even scream.

00:37:30.637 --> 00:37:32.190
How about I send you back there?

00:37:42.508 --> 00:37:43.263
What?

00:37:44.966 --> 00:37:46.533
How did I get here?

00:37:51.916 --> 00:37:55.143
<i>"Key to the Highway" by Big Bill Broonzy</i>

00:37:59.705 --> 00:38:01.373
Demons lie all the time, right?

00:38:01.438 --> 00:38:02.720
Maybe she was lying.

00:38:02.726 --> 00:38:04.773
Come on, is that really what you think?

00:38:07.676 --> 00:38:09.252
How could he do it?

00:38:09.256 --> 00:38:11.470
He did it for you. Exactly.

00:38:11.705 --> 00:38:13.291
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:38:15.128 --> 00:38:16.700
You know, the thought of him,

00:38:18.585 --> 00:38:20.492
Wherever he is right now...

00:38:21.665 --> 00:38:24.063
I mean, he spent his
whole life chasing that

00:38:24.806 --> 00:38:26.762
Yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:38:27.056 --> 00:38:29.012
He should have gone out fighting.

00:38:31.067 --> 00:38:33.143
That was supposed to be his legacy,

00:38:33.145 --> 00:38:34.583
You know?

00:38:36.068 --> 00:38:38.393
Not bargaining with the damn thing.

00:38:40.697 --> 00:38:41.831
Not this.

00:38:41.835 --> 00:38:44.343
How many people do you
think dad saved total?

00:38:44.347 --> 00:38:47.272
That's not the point,
Sam. Evan Hudson is safe

00:38:47.405 --> 00:38:49.373
Because of what dad taught us.

00:38:50.396 --> 00:38:52.031
That's his legacy, Dean.

00:38:53.425 --> 00:38:54.862
Now, we're still here, man,

00:38:54.865 --> 00:38:56.563
So we got to keep going.

00:38:57.395 --> 00:38:58.623
For him.

00:39:05.148 --> 00:39:06.243
Dean? Yeah?

00:39:06.246 --> 00:39:08.143
When you were trapping
that demon, you weren't...

00:39:10.028 --> 00:39:11.873
I mean, it was all a trick, right?

00:39:11.967 --> 00:39:15.000
You never considered actually
making that deal, right?



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
